BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Found Footage Fest: Porcelain VHS Treasures
DTSTART:20260911T020000Z
DTEND:20260911T034500Z
DTSTAMP:20260911T020000Z
UID:0wrIiPLbH1
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nLive comedy with VHS tapes!BRAND 
 NEW VOLUME 11 SHOW FOR 2026! Joe Pickett (The Onion) and Nick Prueher (La
 te Show With David Letterman) have over 14\,000 VHS tapes in their clutter
 ed office in Brooklyn and will take viewers on a guided tour of their late
 st/greatest finds in this brand new Volume 11 show for 2026. Highlights in
 clude a psychotic dollar store salesman\, a video catalog of frightening p
 orcelain dolls\, two wonderfully homemade Bigfoot videos and a new age “
 miracle” treatment from the 80s called “Psychic Surgery.” (Contains 
 nudity\, language\, clowns)“I think I speak for fans everywhere when I e
 xpress gratitude for their continued hunt for hilariously bad videos. I ho
 pe the search never ends.”— Steven Hyden\, Uproxx\n\nhttps://www.siff.
 net/cinema/in-theaters/found-footage-festival-porcelain-vhs-treasures\n\nE
 stimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Faust with the Invincible Czars (1926)
DTSTART:20260910T020000Z
DTEND:20260910T040500Z
DTSTAMP:20260910T020000Z
UID:RE6gW4b3PE
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 106 mins (1h46m)\n\nThe Invincible Czars celebrate 1
 00 years of the silent masterpiece Faust (1926\, FW Murnau). Their brand n
 ew electrifying score marries new and old elements of classical music\, bo
 ssa nova and even a touch of heavy metal to bring the movie to life for co
 ntemporary audiences and incorporates a mix of instruments like flute\, vi
 olin and electric guitar.  Celebrate 100 years of the Uptown with this 
 100 year old film! Free 100 Years of the Uptown stickers to those in atten
 dance.*Live score by The Invincible Czars*\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/
 in-theaters/faust-with-the-invincible-czars\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Breathless (1960)
DTSTART:20260917T023000Z
DTEND:20260917T041500Z
DTSTAMP:20260917T023000Z
UID:gpN6milkw1
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesMichel (Jean-Paul
  Belmondo) stomps the accelerator\, is Parisian-cool\, and casual about th
 e big things (love\, living and dying). Speeding ahead like Bogart in thos
 e American Noir movies\, with the American Patricia (Jean Seberg) sharing 
 his crime spree. She (standing still) gives us a Mona Lisa gaze: all the m
 ysteries.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/nouvelles-femmes/bre
 athless\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Late Fame
DTSTART:20260914T230000Z
DTEND:20260915T005500Z
DTSTAMP:20260914T230000Z
UID:nvGWYZpC0d
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nWillem Dafoe plays a post office 
 employee whose early book of poetry is “rediscovered” by a group of as
 piring artists who adopt him as an elder statesman\, flattering him but al
 so causing him to question their authenticity.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cin
 ema/in-theaters/late-fame\n\nEstimated start: 16:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Serial Mom (1994)
DTSTART:20260915T013000Z
DTEND:20260915T032000Z
DTSTAMP:20260915T013000Z
UID:QEO4Bu7qPq
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 93 mins (1h33m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club Written and dire
 cted by John Waters\, this 1994 dark satirical comedy stars Kathleen Turne
 r as Beverly Sutphin\, a picture-perfect suburban housewife and mother who
  secretly moonlights as a gleeful serial killer. Intro by Graphic Design 
 Manager Rhys Iliakis.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/siff-mov
 ie-club/serial-mom\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
