BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Edie Arnold is a Loser
DTSTART:20260918T020000Z
DTEND:20260918T033000Z
DTSTAMP:20260918T020000Z
UID:rFIFLJBuNK
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 73 mins (1h13m)\n\nJoin us for an exclusive screenin
 g event of the hysterical\, rebellious\, coming of age comedy\, Edie Arnol
 d is a Loser! This SXSW film and SIFF Audience Award Winner follows timid 
 dork Edie as she accidentally takes the spotlight when she starts a punk b
 and with her fellow “turds”\, becoming an icon to the rest of the lose
 rs at her all-girls Catholic school while managing to piss off the hot gir
 ls\, the nuns\, and the horniest altar boy you’ve ever seen. "A sensatio
 nal\, hilarious buddy comedy that will make you want to embrace your inner
  loser." —Mashable "...a coming-of-age story for the weird girls. And th
 ank God." — Kristy Puchko Live Q&A with the Directors Megan Rico & Kade 
 Atwood and Lead Actor Adi Madden Cabrera. Show up early to hang out with t
 he filmmakers and get free merch in the lobby!\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cin
 ema/in-theaters/edie-arnold-is-a-loser\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Center Stage (1991)
DTSTART:20260919T194500Z
DTEND:20260919T223500Z
DTSTAMP:20260919T194500Z
UID:mmc08moCe1
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 154 mins (2h34m)\n\nInternational superstar Maggie C
 heung (In the Mood for Love) embodies tragic screen siren Ruan Lingyu\, kn
 own as the "Greta Garbo of China\," in this unconventional biopic by Hong 
 Kong New Wave master Stanley Kwan (Rouge). New 4K restoration.\n\nhttps:/
 /www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/center-stage\n\nEstimated start: 13:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jules and Jim (1961)
DTSTART:20260924T023000Z
DTEND:20260924T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20260924T023000Z
UID:DyvIK0gD7D
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 105 mins (1h45m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesTwo Parisian lit
 erature-loving friends (Oscar Werner\, Henri Serre) are dumbstruck when th
 ey encounter Catherine (Jeanne Moreau)\, a real-life embodiment of passion
 ate\, adventurous living. Respect and affection flow freely between the th
 ree\, and soon a larking-about friendship branches into many configuration
 s of love.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/nouvelles-femmes/ju
 les-and-jim\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cleo From 5 to 7 (1962)
DTSTART:20261001T023000Z
DTEND:20261001T041500Z
DTSTAMP:20261001T023000Z
UID:1wqNomEtwX
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesThis afternoon\, 
 beautiful pop singer Cléo (Corinne Marchand) will find out the results of
  her cancer biopsy\, and this raw fact changes her life. She’s used to e
 veryone looking adoringly at her\, defining her as a princess. Today\, as 
 Varda says\, “She changes to a black dress\, like singer Edith Piaf\, an
 d goes out\; now she looks at the world.”\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/progra
 ms-and-events/nouvelles-femmes/cleo-from-5-to-7\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Contempt (1963)
DTSTART:20261008T023000Z
DTEND:20261008T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20261008T023000Z
UID:R5NOmEaDHN
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesA film producer 
 (Jack Palance) and his director (pantheon director Fritz Lang) are filming
  Homer’s The Odyssey. The screenwriter (Michel Piccoli) and his stunning
  wife (Brigitte Bardot) are on the scene. Godard seeks to “film thought\
 , the beauty of moments\,” and a small emotional miscalculation (or happ
 enstance) sows doubt in a Mediterranean paradise.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/
 programs-and-events/nouvelles-femmes/contempt\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Carrie (1976)
DTSTART:20261011T223000Z
DTEND:20261012T002500Z
DTSTAMP:20261011T223000Z
UID:XLAEPL8Pc2
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nWelcome to the first installment 
 of SIFF Book Club! We are reading Stephen King's "Carrie" and then watchin
 g it on the big screen for the 50th anniversary.Brian De Palma’s 1976 l
 andmark supernatural horror film\, based on Stephen King’s first novel\,
  resulted in an Oscar® nomination for Sissy Spacek’s portrayal of a tee
 naged social outcast wielding fatal telekinetic powers.  Arrive early to 
 peruse a selection of books from Mercer Street Books. Local artists Chloe 
 Ladwig and Max B will be selling prints\, stickers\, and more featuring th
 e Carrie White. Festival Senior Programmer Dan Doody will be introducing t
 he screening\, providing some book-to-film context before we meet afterwar
 ds for our Book Club discussion at The Traveling Goat.\n\nhttps://www.siff
 .net/programs-and-events/siff-book-club/carrie\n\nEstimated start: 15:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ginger Snaps (2000)
DTSTART:20261013T013000Z
DTEND:20261013T033500Z
DTSTAMP:20261013T013000Z
UID:9WE2YUelBy
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 108 mins (1h48m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club Ginger Snaps is
  a 2000 Canadian supernatural horror film about two death-obsessed sisters
 \, outcasts in their suburban neighborhood\, who must deal with the tragic
  consequences when one of them is bitten by a deadly werewolf. Intro by C
 inema Worker Larcyn Burnett.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/s
 iff-movie-club/ginger-snaps\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Le Bonheur (Happiness) (1965)
DTSTART:20261015T023000Z
DTEND:20261015T040500Z
DTSTAMP:20261015T023000Z
UID:Enp64v38T5
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 80 mins (1h20m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesIn a French Impre
 ssionist landscape of sunny blossoms\, a blissful husband and wife (Jean-C
 laude and Claire Drouot) picnic on the grass. Their happiness feels organi
 cally grown\, part of the natural order. But when Jean-Claude meets a post
 al clerk (Marie-France Boyer)\, he realizes he has a capacity for “more 
 flowers\, more apples.”\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/nouv
 elles-femmes/le-bonheur-(happiness)\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Matchstick Productions Presents\, "The Way Out" 2026 Ski Film
DTSTART:20261021T023000Z
DTEND:20261021T034500Z
DTSTAMP:20261021T023000Z
UID:VT4Y8B8EuK
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 60 mins (1h00m)\n\nMatchstick Productions returns wi
 th their 34th annual ski film\, The Way Out\, a raw tribute to the timeles
 s culture and lifestyle of skiing. Dropping you straight into heavy Alaska
 n spine lines\, deep Japanese powder\, and iconic Swiss villages. This fil
 m shows skiing as far more than a sport\; it’s a path toward total freed
 om. From legendary veterans to rising breakout talent\, the message is sim
 ple: the soul of skiing isn’t dead\; it's waiting wherever snow falls. 
 VIP tickets include premium seating and gift bag from Matchstick Productio
 ns partners.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/matchstick-product
 ions-presents-the-way-out-2026-ski-film\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Hitcher (1986)
DTSTART:20261016T020000Z
DTEND:20261016T035500Z
DTSTAMP:20261016T020000Z
UID:PxCaq8rbON
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 97 mins (1h37m)\n\nOn a dark and stormy night\, fati
 gued driver Jim Halsey (C. Thomas Howell) picks up a mysterious hitchhiker
  (Rutger Hauer)\, leading to a terrifying cat-and-mouse nightmare along th
 e highways of the American southwest.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and
 -events/the-open-road/the-hitcher\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Band of Outsiders (1964)
DTSTART:20261022T023000Z
DTEND:20261022T042000Z
DTSTAMP:20261022T023000Z
UID:X5lfrHskLW
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesGodard puts his a
 ppreciative-playful spin on Hollywood-style Noir. Two guys (Claude Brasseu
 r\, Sami Frey) team with a lovely\, naive\, doe-eyed language student (Ann
 a Karina) to steal money that’s hidden in her rooming house. Karina conv
 eys a woman coming into her exuberant selfhood. When the three line dance 
 the Madison\, she keeps going\, bouncing and smiling.\n\nhttps://www.siff.
 net/programs-and-events/nouvelles-femmes/band-of-outsiders\n\nEstimated st
 art: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CatVideoFest 2026
DTSTART:20261030T020000Z
DTEND:20261030T034500Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T020000Z
UID:SFlwuShUal
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nSpecial encore screening for Nati
 onal Cat Day! The world's #1 cat video festival is back with screenings i
 n theaters across the USA and around the world. A portion of ticket sales
  will support PAWS (​​Progressive Animal Welfare Society). NEKO Cat C
 afe will be tabling in the lobby before showtime. 🐱\n\nhttps://www.siff
 .net/cinema/in-theaters/cat-vid-fest-26\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stolen Kisses (1968)
DTSTART:20261029T023000Z
DTEND:20261029T041500Z
DTSTAMP:20261029T023000Z
UID:HK7dlip3HJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nNouvelles FemmesTruffaut's alter-
 ego Antoine Doinel (Jean-Pierre Léaud) gains access to the hearts of Pari
 s by becoming a detective. He’s emotionally up and down with his girlfri
 end Christine (Claude Jade) but the endearingly hapless fellow is instantl
 y smitten by the elegant wife (Delphine Seyrig) of a client.\n\nhttps://ww
 w.siff.net/programs-and-events/nouvelles-femmes/stolen-kisses\n\nEstimated
  start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Man and A Woman (1966)
DTSTART:20261105T033000Z
DTEND:20261105T053000Z
DTSTAMP:20261105T033000Z
UID:ymZEn68mqm
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nNouvelles Femmes60th Anniversary
  Screening. A man (Jean-Louis Trintignant) and a woman\, (Anouk Aimée)\,
  who’ve painfully lost their loves\, meet by chance. They’re very appe
 aling to each other (and to us)\, but can current attraction overcome past
  memories? Aimee’s enigmatic face has answers. This film played for 82 s
 traight weeks in Seattle.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/nouv
 elles-femmes/a-man-and-a-woman\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Discreet Charm of the Bourgeoisie (1972)
DTSTART:20261110T023000Z
DTEND:20261110T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20261110T023000Z
UID:raujo4vZk7
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club 4K restoration.
  A group of six friends - three men and three women decidedly of the Frenc
 h Upper Middle Class - have their dinner plans continually interrupted due
  to a series of bizarre events that can only be described as Buñuelian. I
 ntro by Graphic Design Manager Rhys Iliakis.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/progr
